  "question": {
    "text": "A thin prism <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> with an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and made of glass of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>54</mn></math> is combined with another prism <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> made from glass of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>72</mn></math> to produce dispersion without average deviation. The angle of prism <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is :"
